The Export Browsing Data interface.

•	The interface is visually organized into four principal areas: the Cancel button, the main heading and explicatory text, the list of data categories to be exported, and the Save to Downloads button:
o	Cancel: a blue colored text borderless button position on the top left of the interface
	Primary Heading: Centrally aligned, in large-sized, bold black letters "Export Browsing Data."
	Centered, in normal-sized black text, the following text:
- First Paragraph: Export selected browser data as an archive to allow importing into other browsers. 
- Second Paragraph: Your data will be saved without encryption and will be visible to anyone who can access the exported file. 
o	The list of data type items, each with selection circle-mark, an icon that reflect the type of data, the name of the type of data, and the number of stored items of that data type:
	Bookmarks
- Checked
- Book blue icon
- 4 bookmarks
	History
- Unchecked
- Clock icon
- 0 sites
	Extensions
- Unchecked
- Puzzle piece icon
- 0 extensions
	Credit Cards
- Unchecked
- Credit Card icon
- 0 cards
	Passwords
- Unchecked
- Key icon
- 0 passwords
o	Save to Downloads button: spanning the width of the screen in white letters and blue background
